# SightLine API keys
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the project root (or to %APPDATA%/SightLine/.env).
# Keys are read at startup and the Anthropic, OpenAI and ElevenLabs keys are
# saved encrypted on this PC (Electron safeStorage, which uses Windows DPAPI)
# in %APPDATA%/SightLine/keys.json, so you only need this file once. The
# Google values are read from this file on every start. After changing a key
# here, restart SightLine. `.env` is gitignored — never commit real keys.

# ── Required ──
# The coach itself. Without this, nothing works.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ── Voice out (at least one strongly recommended) ──
# ElevenLabs is the one that makes the coach sound like a person, and it's the
# fastest — roughly 4x quicker to first audio than the alternatives. The app
# falls back automatically: ElevenLabs → Google → OpenAI → the robotic system
# voice, so a missing key degrades quality rather than breaking anything.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Google Cloud Text-to-Speech (Chirp 3 HD). Service-account credentials.
# Note: paste the private key with literal \n escapes, on one line.
GOOGLE_PROJECT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_EMAIL=
GOOGLE_PRIVATE_KEY=

# ── Voice in + backup voice out ──
# Whisper transcription for hold-to-talk, and the last cloud TTS fallback.
# Without this, the mic and push-to-talk are unavailable (typing still works).
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ── Not yet wired (see docs/PRODUCTION.md) ──
# Everything persists locally today. These are the hooks for the hosted
# version; leaving them empty is the supported configuration.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://...@...neon.tech/sightline?sslmode=require
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# AWS_S3_BUCKET=
